Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Use a VBT with DisplayPort on DDI B

coreboot bug #670: the VBT described its first external output as
DVI/HDMI on DDI B (device type 0x60d2, HDMI-B, no AUX channel), but the
DisplayPort connector of these boards is on DDI B and the HDMI one on
DDI C. i915 then made an HDMI connector out of the DisplayPort one and a
DP monitor there was not detected; the HDMI port worked as DDI C was
DP++. The M920x has the same rear outputs (one HDMI, one DisplayPort,
the optional port on DDI D).

The in-tree VBT is one of the 19 of the OEM firmware, for another SKU.
This one, made for the bug by Matt DeVillier from the OEM tables:
DP-B with AUX-B (0x60d6), HDMI-C (0x60d2), DP++ on DDI D for the
optional port, no phantom LFP1 and no fixed 1024x768 boot mode, at
BDB 228 as the Coffee Lake FSP sample. Tested in the bug on an M720q
with libgfxinit: DP and HDMI in EDK2 and in Linux, and after S3.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x. On the M920x: HDMI in the firmware and in
Linux as before, in the hardware test; DP not tried (no cable).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
